# Keeps content/bre/ in the bundle.
#
# The scaffold ships this tree EMPTY on purpose: no demo data, so nothing from another
# engagement can leak into a customer deliverable. But an empty directory is not a thing
# git can carry, and it does not survive most archive-and-copy paths either — so without
# this file the directory disappears the moment the skill is committed or packaged, and
# step 5's `cp -R <bre-source>/. content/bre/` fails for everyone but the author.
#
# Step 5 fills this from the BRE source (e.g. business-rules-extraction/). Leave the file
# in place; build-embed.js ignores dotfiles.
